$\ndet(T)=4\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 2=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,2\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-11977" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8f12f67c515551308fa247bf9f644c620d693c31d1b5e9f062904df55636ee"} {"question" "q-11977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-11977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "3"] ["math" "5"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-11977" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-12279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/f24ec004411065e89b68793e32c80231c7eff6f9ff31e46bc530f78c9c270064.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-12279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 7\\cdot 4=14.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=5\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot (-4)=7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,7\\,|\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =98.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-12279" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8f12f67c515551308fa247bf9f644c620d693c31d1b5e9f062904df55636ee"} {"question" "q-12279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-12279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "100"] ["math" "102"] ["math" "9"] ["math" "98"] ["math" "99"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-12279" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "98"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/dbda6ab548ce83f1b2c2d74cf08c2ec01ea7de089bb36f8e0c98985a432202d1.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=4\\cdot 2=8.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-1)\\cdot 1-2\\cdot 3=-7.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-7\\,|\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =56.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316592" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8f12f67c515551308fa247bf9f644c620d693c31d1b5e9f062904df55636ee"} {"question" "q-316592" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316592" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "56"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The unit square $D$ has vertices $(1,0),(0,0),(0,1),(1,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/6805467a24cb40559f205cbfcecc4f5a34ff2ec6ebda8ae67f997c02f123b53c.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-4)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 1=-12-2=-14.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,-14\\,|\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316598" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "8d8f12f67c515551308fa247bf9f644c620d693c31d1b5e9f062904df55636ee"} {"question" "q-316598" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316598" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "14"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The triangle $D$ has vertices $(2,2),(5,2),(4,5).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $T$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n$\\text{Area}(T(D))=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316609" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/assets/aef99dd5276166e5c7b4fb2f716b060390b6577f2d3625dd5dc835bcec6c4856.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $T,$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $T(D)$ under the action of $T:$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(T(D))=|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D).\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D)=\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 3\\cdot 3=\\frac{9}{2}.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\ndet(T)=(-5)\\cdot (-2)-0\\cdot 0=10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot \\frac{9}{2} \\\\  & =45.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14064490/state.json" "file_sha256" "d15a4e5044f1a7f0a157391ee0b585e0092ecfba8bd67031e18b988bb2ef5344"} {"question" "q-316609" "field"